<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!-- pacs.009 COV — a cover payment. The banks settle between themselves the
     money of a customer transfer that travelled separately as a pacs.008, and
     <UndrlygCstmrCdtTrf> names that underlying customer debtor and creditor.

     MT202COV exists because its predecessor let the customer names disappear
     on the interbank leg, which made cover payments a money-laundering
     corridor; a reader that drops the block reproduces exactly the opacity the
     format was created to remove. The parties of the transfer itself are
     BANKS (FinInstnId), which is why the columns say debtor_fi/creditor_fi.
     Shape from the payments-maintenance COV samples carried by Nivaes and
     Payment-Components. -->
